/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak
.DS_Store

# Built locally by editors/vscode/install.ps1
*.vsix

# What a compiled Khora program leaves beside its source, and what the link
# shortener writes while it runs.
examples/**/src/*.exe
examples/**/src/*.o
# Debug information, since 12.4: a PDB beside the executable on Windows, and
# the IR dump `KHORA_EMIT_LLVM` asks for.
examples/**/src/*.pdb
examples/**/src/*.ll
examples/**/links.txt

# The benchmark servers, built by hand rather than by cargo.
bench/**/src/*.exe
bench/**/src/*.o
bench/**/src/*.pdb
bench/**/src/*.ll
bench/*.exe
bench/*.pdb

# What `khora test` and `khora bench` leave beside the sources they compiled.
# `std/khora-tests.exe` was committed — 3.5 MB of build output inside the
# standard library — because these are written into the directory under test
# and nothing here named them.
**/khora-tests
**/khora-tests.exe
**/khora-tests.exe.o
**/khora-tests.pdb
**/khora-benches
**/khora-benches.exe
**/khora-benches.exe.o
**/khora-benches.pdb

# Written by `scripts/setup-llvm.sh`; `.cargo/config.toml.example` is the
# template. It names an LLVM prefix and a Windows SDK version, both of which
# differ per machine.
/.cargo/config.toml

# The baseline's receipt. `scripts/baseline.sh` writes it on success and
# `scripts/gate.sh` reads it; it names a working tree, so it is meaningless on
# any other machine and belongs to nobody's history.
/.khora-gate-full
/.khora-gate-fast

# The peer servers `bench/compare.py` measures against, built by hand from
# `bench/peers/`. Sources are tracked; binaries and build trees are not.
/bench/peers/*.exe
/bench/peers/*.class
/bench/peers/dotnet_health/bin/
/bench/peers/dotnet_health/obj/
/bench/*/src/release.exe
/bench/*/src/release.exe.o
/bench/*/src/release.pdb
/bench/compare.json

# What `scripts/package.sh` assembles. Built on demand and published by the
# release workflow; never committed.
/dist/
